## Tutorials

Thez-indexproperty specifies the stack order of 
positioned elements.

The stack order defines which element should be placed in front or behind other 
elements.

When elements are positioned, they can overlap other elements.

An element can have a positive or negative stack order (z-index):

Note:z-indexonly works onpositioned elements(position: absolute, 
position: relative, position: fixed, or position: sticky) andflex items(elements that are direct children of display: flex elements).

A positioned element with a greater stack order is always above an element 
with a lower stack order.

If several positioned elements overlap each other without az-indexspecified, the elements render in the order they are defined in the HTML source 
code.

### Code Examples

